            <div class="terms-section" id="your-rights">
                <div class="terms-section-number">8</div>
                <h2>Your Rights Under the Data Privacy Act</h2>
                <p>As a data subject under Republic Act No. 10173, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
                <ul class="terms-list">
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">1</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to be informed</strong> — You have the right to be informed of the collection and processing of your personal data, including the purpose, scope, and method of processing, as well as the identity of the personal information controller.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">2</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to access</strong> — You may request a copy of your personal data that we hold, the sources from which it was obtained, the recipients or classes of recipients to whom it has been disclosed, and the manner by which it was processed.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">3</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to object</strong> — You may object to the processing of your personal data, including processing for direct marketing, automated processing, or profiling. We will cease processing upon receipt of a valid objection, unless we have compelling legitimate grounds.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">4</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to erasure or blocking</strong> — You may request the removal or blocking of your personal data if it is incomplete, outdated, false, unlawfully obtained, no longer necessary for the declared purpose, or if you withdraw your consent.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">5</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — You may dispute and request the correction of any inaccurate or erroneous personal data we hold about you.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">6</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — You may request a copy of your personal data in an electronic or structured format that allows further use, and have it transmitted to another personal information controller where technically feasible.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">7</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to file a complaint</strong> — If you believe your data privacy rights have been violated, you have the right to file a complaint with the National Privacy Commission.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="terms-list-icon">8</span>
                        <span><strong>Right to damages</strong> — You may claim compensation for damages sustained as a result of inaccurate, incomplete, outdated, false, unlawfully obtained, or unauthorized use of your personal data.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact our Data Protection Officer at <strong>dpo&#64;bookmeapp.ph</strong>. We will respond to your request within <strong>fifteen (15) business days</strong> from receipt of a complete and verified request, in accordance with NPC guidelines.</p>
